      "description": "Watch Kilmarnock vs ST Mirren highlights and goals from Premiership - Scotland on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 2, 2026. The Scottish Premiership delivered an intense battle on September 2, 2026 , as Kilmarnock hosted St. Mirren . Both sides entered the pitch looking to establish their dominance in a fixture characterized by tactical discipline and high physical stakes. Early Breakthrough for the Visitors The match ignited almost immediately, with the visiting side finding their rhythm within the opening moments. In the 4th minute, St. Mirren stunned the home crowd when Nikolas Agrafiotis delivered a pinpoint assist to find Fraser Taylor . Taylor made no mistake, firing the ball home to give his side an early lead. This clinical start forced Kilmarnock into a chasing position early on, as they struggled to break down a well-organized opposition defense. As the first half progressed, the atmosphere grew increasingly combative. The referee was forced to reach for his pocket multiple times to maintain order, issuing yellow cards to St. Mirren 's Greg Kiltie in the 38th minute and Nikolas Agrafiotis shortly before the break. Despite the rising tension, the scoreline remained unchanged heading into the interval. Defensive Resilience and Tactical Shifts The second half saw a flurry of tactical changes as both managers looked to influence the outcome. Kilmarnock introduced Jamie Brandon , Aaron Tshibola , and Djenairo Daniels at the restart to inject energy into their play. St. Mirren responded with their own substitutions, bringing on the likes of Jake Young and Rory McKenzie to solidify their structure and protect their narrow advantage. The closing stages were marked by further disciplinary action, reflecting the desperation of the final minutes. In the 82nd minute, both Jayden Richardson and Bailey Rice received yellow cards as the physical battles intensified across the pitch. Despite late pressure from the hosts, the final whistle after four minutes of stoppage time confirmed a hard-fought victory for St. Mirren , secured by that decisive early strike."
