      "description": "Watch ST Mirren vs Motherwell highlights and goals from Premiership - Scotland on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 30, 2026. The Scottish Premiership clash between St. Mirren and Motherwell delivered everything a football fan could ask for in a high-stakes encounter. In an afternoon defined by constant momentum shifts, both sides displayed a relentless attacking spirit that kept the result in doubt until the final seconds. Early Breakthrough and Penalty Drama The match burst into life on August 30, 2026, as Motherwell wasted no time establishing their presence. Just 2 minutes in, Tawanda Maswanhise found the back of the net following a sharp assist from Alex Lowry . The visitors had a golden chance to double their lead in the 14th minute when a penalty was awarded, but Maswanhise failed to convert, providing St. Mirren with a much-needed lifeline. St. Mirren’s Resurgence and First-Half Flurry Capitalizing on the missed penalty, the home side rallied. Regan Charles-Cook restored parity in the 24th minute, and the turnaround seemed complete when Paul Nsio made it 2-1 in the 39th minute, assisted by Samuel Ramos . The goal-fest continued just before the break; Declan John leveled for Motherwell in the 44th minute, only for Samuel Ramos to strike back for St. Mirren in first-half stoppage time, assisted by Alexandros Gogic , sent the hosts into the locker room with a 3-2 lead. Late Drama and Kanga's Equalizer The second half saw a tighter contest as tactical adjustments and defensive caution took center stage. Yellow cards were brandished for Stephen O'Donnell , Martin Moormann , Ryan Carr , and Jake Young as the intensity remained high. As the clock ticked into stoppage time, Motherwell launched one final assault. In the 90+3rd minute, substitute Jardell Kanga emerged as the hero, firing home to secure a dramatic 3-3 draw and ensuring both teams walked away with a point from this classic football match."
